mise run test           # build, then ctest under the sanitizers
mise run lint           # clang-format --dry-run, clang-tidy
mise run fmt            # clang-format -i
{%- elif stack == 'rust' %}
mise run test           # cargo nextest, doctests{% if frontend %}, vitest{% endif %}
mise run lint           # cargo fmt --check, clippy, cargo deny, cargo machete{% if frontend %}, biome check, tsc --noEmit{% endif %}
mise run fmt            # cargo fmt{% if frontend %}, biome format{% endif %}
{%- if frontend %}
mise run fe:dev         # Vite dev server
mise run fe:build       # build into frontend/dist
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
mise run check-commits  # cocogitto on unpushed commits
```

## Structure

- Build deep modules: a small interface over much hidden work. No pass-through wrappers, barrel files or `utils` grab bags.
{%- if stack == 'python' %}
- A package exports its public names through `__init__.py` and `__all__`. Other modules import those names and reach no deeper.
{%- elif stack == 'typescript' %}
- A module exports its public names from one entry file. Other modules import those names and reach no deeper.
{%- elif stack == 'cpp' %}
- A module's public names live in one header. Other modules include that header and reach no deeper.
- Modern C++20: RAII, `std::unique_ptr` over `new`, no raw owning pointers. A sanitizer finding is a bug, never noise.
- `.clang-tidy` turns every finding into an error. Turn a check off there, with the reason, not with `NOLINT` in the code.
{%- elif stack == 'rust' %}
- A module's public names are its `pub` items. Other modules use those and reach no deeper; keep the rest private or `pub(crate)`.
- Clippy warnings are errors. Turn a lint off under `[lints]` in `Cargo.toml`, with the reason, not with `#[allow]` in the code.
- `cargo deny` fails on a dependency whose licence is not in `deny.toml`, and `cargo machete` on one the code does not use.
{%- if frontend %}
- The frontend is Effect UI, a preview whose API still changes. Read `frontend/node_modules/@effect/ui/AGENTS.md` before writing a component: it is the guide for the installed version.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
- At most about 7 entries per folder; above that, group by concept into a subfolder with one entry point. `scripts/check-fan-out` enforces it, with `.fan-out-baseline` for accepted overages and `.fan-out-excludes` for folders that are lists by design.
- No file passes 5000 tokens (bytes/4); `scripts/check-file-size` enforces it. A Claude Code hook in `.claude/settings.json` runs both checks on each edit.

## Comments and pull requests

- Names and structure explain the code. A comment says only what the code cannot: a limit from outside it (a spec, a hardware or library quirk) or a reason that would surprise a reader. No comment restates the code, narrates the change or tells its history.
{%- if stack != 'none' %}
- `scripts/check-comments` fails on a comment a change adds, on commit, push and in CI. It lets through license headers, tool directives (`noqa`, `biome-ignore`, `NOLINT` ...), doc comments (`/**`, `///`) and a comment that links the spec, issue or vendor doc it follows. Turn a "do not change" comment into a type, lint rule or test instead. Generated or vendored code goes in `.comments-excludes`. In Claude Code, `/pstack:no-comments` (the pstack plugin) reviews a diff by the same rule.
{%- endif %}
- The pull request explains the change. Under "Changes" in its body, show each change that needs explaining as a short excerpt of the code, say why it looks that way, and link the docs, spec or issue it follows.

## Conventions

- Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:` ...). The `commit-msg` hook rejects anything else.
- Default branch is `{{ default_branch }}`. With branch protection applied (`mise run repo:apply-settings`), changes land through PRs that pass Lint,{% if stack != 'none' %} Test,{% endif %} Commits, Review and Security.
- Before a commit that changes behaviour, run the `verify` skill (`.claude/skills/verify/SKILL.md`) and put what it shows under Testing in the pull request.
- An issue says what shows it is finished under "Done when" (`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/task.md`), also when you open it with `gh`. A pull request's body shows the command and output that prove it, says what no check covers, and lists what the change decided that the issue did not.
- Review and Security are Claude reviews in CI. They follow `REVIEW.md`; answer every Important thread before the merge. A PR that touches a path in `.github/CODEOWNERS` also needs a code owner's review.
- Every `uses:` in a workflow names a full commit SHA, with the version as a comment. The repo refuses an action on a tag, and any action whose owner is not in `.github/selected-actions.json`. Dependabot updates the SHAs.
- Update from the Copier template with `uvx copier update`.
